Ceratodon is a genus of mosses belonging to the family Ditrichaceae. The genus was first described by Samuel Elisée Bridel-Brideri and has a cosmopolitan distribution.

Species
The following species are recognised in the genus Ceratodon:
{{div col|colwidth=22em}} 
Ceratodon amazonum {{small|Nieto-Lugilde, O.Werner, S.F.McDaniel & Ros}}
Ceratodon bryophilus {{small|Besch.}}
Ceratodon conicus {{small|(Hampe ex Müll.Hal.) Lindb.}}
Ceratodon graefii {{small|Schlieph.}}
Ceratodon heterophyllus {{small|Kindb.}}
Ceratodon purpureus {{small|(Hedw.) Brid.}}
{{div col end}}
